{
	title: 'Theme selection uses a portable ordinary plugin file',
	spec: `Replace /theme-managed symlinks with an ordinary portable plugin, plugins/theme.ts. It re-exports a shipped theme by relative path, e.g. export { default } from '../themes/nostromo.ts' (the home is the checkout; HAL_HOME is for tests only), plus export const portable = true. Its small readable contents select a shipped themes/<name>.ts registration function, so a client/server diff clearly shows nostromo versus wopr rather than an entire palette or machine-specific link. Preserve task d3's theme choices, question UI, color rules, hook cleanup and redraw semantics; keys remain readable one-override-per-key plugins as task 8kx specifies, with portable metadata documented for both examples.

/theme recognizes and atomically rewrites its managed selector. Safely convert an existing recognized plugins/color-theme.ts theme symlink into plugins/theme.ts without changing the selected theme or overwriting its target. Preserve custom plugin contents and unknown symlinks; refuse to overwrite them with a clear explanation. Built-in hal selection has an unambiguous representation consistent with d3's removal behavior and history tombstones. Shipped-theme changes still reach a selector on subsequent load; theme implementation files are not automatically transferred with the selector. Missing themes report a complete load error, never silently select another theme. No private plugin contents or host paths enter tracked artifacts. Test known-link migration, custom-file preservation, switching and missing theme behavior. This supersedes d3's symlink requirement; it does not change palette values or add web behavior. hal/intro (task vc) offers the theme question as a first-run step and writes plugins/theme.ts with the default selection; changing the answer switches the theme live.`,
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['d3', '8kx', 'gev', 'vc'],
	foldInto: ['d3']
}
